# Device developer review standard

When running the agent review step of the iam-device-developer workflow, apply this checklist to changed code:

## Code quality

- [ ] Logic is correct and handles edge cases; no obvious bugs.
- [ ] Error handling is present where needed (e.g. validation, external calls); errors are meaningful.
- [ ] Code follows existing patterns in `devices/src/` and project style (e.g. naming, structure).
- [ ] No unrelated or debug code left in; no commented-out blocks that should be removed.
- [ ] Functions are focused and reasonably sized; complexity is acceptable.

## Tests and docs

- [ ] New or changed behavior has corresponding unit tests in `devices/tests/`.
- [ ] Public interfaces or non-obvious behavior have brief docstrings where appropriate.
- [ ] `devices/docs/` is consistent with the changes — run the `update-devices-docs` skill if any filter pipeline, routing, or validator logic changed.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Every acceptance criterion from the Jira story is mapped to implementation or tests; list each AC and confirm Done or Not done.

Fix any issues found before asking the user for approval to commit.
